.TH LOCK 1 "2026-09-20" "caveutils" "caveutils Manual"
.SH NAME
lock \- real screen lock - invokes this project's own already-vendored
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lock
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lock
.nf
suckless slock (coreutils/slock/, real, already built - checked by
hand) instead of reimplementing a screen locker. Falls back to a
plain `slock` on PATH if the vendored build isn't reachable (e.g.
this script copied somewhere the repo layout doesn't match).
.fi
